[en.C14_APPLEPIE]
Applepie Republic

[en.C14_APPLEPIE_DEF]
Applepie Republic

[en.C14_APPLEPIE_ADJ]
Applepie Family

[en.C14_DESC]
The apple family is once the most influence family in Equestria, no doubt. But after the Ultimate Battle, the glory days of the apple family are gone.\nFortunately, the vitality of the apple family is tenacious - as one of the oldest families in Equestria, they have survived countless troughs and are still standing today. The apple family has close ties with the Pie family, the Pear family and other families. With their help, the apple family has managed to keep their gathering town - Appleloosa - during the Ultimate Battle and the following years. In the spring of 1001, under the operation of the family, the mayor of Appleloosa appointed by the Royal Commission was forced to step down, and Braeburn and his apple family regained control of Appleloosa.\nAs Appleloosa is still in recovery, Braeburn and his family members have postponed the retaliation against old enemies, and instead focused on restoring the economy and agriculture of Appleloosa. They are now facing Ponyville and the Equestria Empire with a cooperative attitude. But at the same time, Braeburn is also secretly intensifying military and economic cooperation with the Pie family. He knows very well that the apple family will eventually regain its position and like old times, raise the barn, again.

[en.PIHC_WS_C14_desc]
The apple family is once the most influence family in Equestria, no doubt. In the town of Appleloosa, generations of apple ponies were raised; in the apple farm of Ponyville, many acres of land are owned by the apple family; apples, apple ciders, apple pies and zap apples are sold to every corner of Equestria... But after the Ultimate Battle, the glory days of the apple family are gone, the influence of the family is waning, and the town of Appleloosa, which once flourished with the gathering of the apple family, has become a town in decline. The cold winter has hit the apple trees, the war has destroyed the peaceful market for apples, and the regional separatism has cut off the connection between the family members scattered throughout Equestria. The agricultural reform has led Ponyville, the village founded by the ancestors of the apple family, to abandon its former bloodline. Many family members have either met with misfortune or disappeared.\n\nFortunately, the vitality of the apple family is tenacious - as one of the oldest families in Equestria, they have survived countless troughs and are still standing today. The apple family has close ties with the Pie family, the Pear family and other families. With their help, the apple family has managed to keep their gathering town - Appleloosa - during the Ultimate Battle and the following years. After Applejack was arrested, Big Mac and Apple Bloom disappeared, Braeburn, known as the “Cousin”, became the de facto leader of the apple family. Under his leadership, the influence of the apple family has strategically shrunk on the continent of Equestria, stabilizing their local power in Southern Equestria. In the spring of 1001, under the operation of the family, the mayor of Appleloosa appointed by the Royal Commission was forced to step down, and then disappeared. Braeburn and his apple family regained control of Appleloosa. There was a little bloodshed in the process, but not much.\n\nAs Appleloosa is still in recovery, Braeburn and his family members have postponed the retaliation against old enemies, and instead focused on restoring the economy and agriculture of Appleloosa. They are now facing Ponyville and the Equestria Empire with a cooperative attitude. But at the same time, Braeburn is also secretly intensifying military and economic cooperation with the Pie family. He knows very well that the apple family will eventually regain its position and like old times, raise the barn, again.

